From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:04:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: apple: Keep the T8132 USB3 PHY out of P3 in host
 mode

On the J713 a SuperSpeed link does not come back from U3 once the core
has suspended the USB3 PHY with it (GUSB3PIPECTL.SUSPHY): resuming the
port drops the link, and the whole tree behind it disconnects. This
happens when a USB3 hub autosuspends, and on every resume from
suspend-to-idle, where the USB core suspends all ports. A mounted disk
behind a USB3 hub is removed under its filesystem.

Clear SUSPHY for the USB3 PHY once the T8132 PIPE switch to USB3 is
done, by setting dis_u3_susphy_quirk, which dwc3_enable_susphy() then
honours when the xHCI host starts. The switch itself still runs with
SUSPHY set, as it requires. Restore the device tree's setting before the
host is stopped, which sets SUSPHY again: the PHY hands the PIPE back in
P3, and fails to lock the PIPE handler otherwise. The core stop does the
same for the error paths.

USB2 PHY suspend is unchanged. The port routes the USB3 PIPE for any
USB-C device in USB mode, so the USB3 PHY stays out of P3 while any USB
device is attached, also a USB 2.0 one. The idle USB-C ports are
powered down, so it costs nothing with nothing attached.

The host test stubs of struct dwc3 and struct dwc3_apple gain
dis_u3_susphy_quirk and dt_dis_u3_susphy, and the teardown test checks
that the device tree's setting is back before the host exits.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(backported from commit 9ec757d1fbe6bddafbd0ef69b9fa318bd5da7377)
[j604: driver change identical to upstream (16+). Context: the base has
 no host-only T6040 support (a50abc4f7b) nor the T6040 controller
 tunables/PIPE reset (205c92374f), so those neighbouring lines are left
 out. The host-test stub hunks (tools/asahi/neo-stability-tests.py,
 selftests apple-dcp dwc3/mocks.c and teardown_pm.py) are not taken: this
 tree's stubs lack the T6040/T8132 fields they extend (TO-VERIFY: those
 host tests are not run here).]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
index 150d3d01e3..f0e8008d65 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@
  * @idle_rpm: Let the controller runtime-suspend while the core is down
  * @rpm_held: The glue holds a runtime PM reference for the running core
  * @pre_core_rpm: Runtime PM is the glue's own until the first core bring-up
+ * @dt_dis_u3_susphy: The device tree keeps USB3 PHY suspend off itself
  */
 struct dwc3_apple {
 	struct dwc3 dwc;
@@ -145,6 +146,7 @@ struct dwc3_apple {
 	bool idle_rpm;
 	bool rpm_held;
 	bool pre_core_rpm;
+	bool dt_dis_u3_susphy;
 };
 
 #define to_dwc3_apple(d) container_of((d), struct dwc3_apple, dwc)
@@ -328,6 +330,8 @@ static int dwc3_apple_core_stop(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc)
 	lockdep_assert_held(&appledwc->lock);
 	if (appledwc->core_active) {
 		if (!appledwc->core_exit_pending) {
+			/* The PHY hands the PIPE back in P3, as it took it over */
+			dwc->dis_u3_susphy_quirk = appledwc->dt_dis_u3_susphy;
 			dwc3_enable_susphy(dwc, true);
 			dwc3_event_buffers_cleanup(dwc);
 			appledwc->core_exit_pending = true;
@@ -495,6 +499,7 @@ static int dwc3_apple_set_role(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc, enum dwc3_apple_stat
 	 * device mode and the T8132 host role were selected in dwc3_apple_core_start();
 	 * other host roles are selected by the xHCI root hub as it starts.
 	 */
+	appledwc->dwc.dis_u3_susphy_quirk = appledwc->dt_dis_u3_susphy;
 	dwc3_enable_susphy(&appledwc->dwc, true);
 	ret = phy_set_mode(appledwc->usb3_phy, host ? PHY_MODE_USB_HOST : PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE);
 	if (ret) {
@@ -502,6 +507,14 @@ static int dwc3_apple_set_role(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc, enum dwc3_apple_stat
 		if (of_device_is_compatible(appledwc->dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-dwc3"))
 			return ret;
 		dev_warn(appledwc->dev, "USB3 PHY setup failed, USB2 only, err=%d\n", ret);
+	} else if (host && appledwc->usb3_phy &&
+		   of_device_is_compatible(appledwc->dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-dwc3")) {
+		/*
+		 * The T8132 PHY does not bring a SuperSpeed link back from U3 once
+		 * the core has suspended it: keep it out of P3 from here on.
+		 */
+		appledwc->dwc.dis_u3_susphy_quirk = true;
+		dwc3_enable_susphy(&appledwc->dwc, true);
 	}
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -578,6 +591,8 @@ static int dwc3_apple_exit(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc)
 		appledwc->state = DWC3_APPLE_NO_CABLE;
 		break;
 	case DWC3_APPLE_HOST:
+		/* dwc3_host_exit() lets the USB3 PHY into P3 for the PIPE handback */
+		appledwc->dwc.dis_u3_susphy_quirk = appledwc->dt_dis_u3_susphy;
 		dwc3_host_exit(&appledwc->dwc);
 		appledwc->state = DWC3_APPLE_NO_CABLE;
 		break;
@@ -695,6 +710,7 @@ static int dwc3_apple_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	appledwc->dev = &pdev->dev;
 	appledwc->fixed_hub = dwc3_apple_has_fixed_hub(dev);
+	appledwc->dt_dis_u3_susphy = device_property_read_bool(dev, "snps,dis_u3_susphy_quirk");
 	/* The PHY driver and the DARTs follow runtime PM on these SoCs. */
 	appledwc->idle_rpm = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t6040-dwc3") ||
 			     of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-dwc3");
